# Now the hidden area should have swung shut.

# NOT a game bug -- the tightest timing window in the corpus so
# far, and the five-minute wait was fatal generosity. Traced in
# the object tree: George slips into the closet at 12:18, dials
# the safe open, reads the new will, relocks everything, and is
# at the top of the stairs by 12:27 -- and the safe has no
# combination you will ever learn, so what locks then locks for
# good. The walkthroughs' "take will / look in safe" assume you
# burst in DURING his visit. To the minute: south to the library,
# examine the bookshelf (this is what reveals the button --
# pressing blind finds nothing), wait exactly two minutes while
# George finishes dialing -- press during the dialing and he
# panics, bolts, and the safe stays shut forever -- then press.
# The shelf swings out on George mid-triumph: he crumples,
# sobbing, clutching the new will beside the wide-open safe, and
# the button-press itself carries you into the closet.

s
examine the bookshelf
wait
wait
press the button

# The will comes off the sobbing heir ("disowning George and
# giving his entire estate to his wife"). The safe needs a "look
# in" before its contents come into reach -- and taking the stack
# overloads your arms, fumbling something to the floor every
# time, so the cup gets parked here first (the closet keeps it if
# it is ever wanted again).

take new will
look in safe
drop cup
take stack
read papers

